{title: 003 - God Himself Is With Us}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: Gerhard Tersteegen}
{composer: Joachim Neander}
{key: G}
{time: 2/2}
{tempo: 96}
{tag: Worship}
{tag: Adoration and Praise}

Verse 1:
[G]God Himself is [D]with us; [Em/B]Let us all adore [Bm]Him,
[C/G]And with [G]awe appear before [D]Him.
[G]God is here within [D]us; [Em/B]Soul, in silence [Bm]fear Him,
[C/G]Humbly, [G]fervently draw [D]near Him.
[G]Now His [C/E]own [D7]who have [G]known [Bm]God, in worship [D7/C]lowly,
[Bm]Yield their [D7/C]spirits wholly.

Verse 2:
[G]Come, abide within [D]me; [Em/B]Let my soul, like [Bm]Mary,
[C/G]Be Thine [G]earthly sanctuary.
[G]Come, indwelling [D]Spirit, [Em/B]With transfigured [Bm]splendor;
[C/G]Love and [G]honor will I [D]render.
[G]Where I [C/E]go [D7]here below, [Bm]Let me bow before [D7/C]Thee,
[Bm]Know Thee [D7/C]and adore Thee.

Verse 3:
[G]Gladly we surrender [D]Earth's [Em/B]deceitful treasures,
[C/G]Pride of [G]life and sinful [D]pleasures:
[G]Gladly, Lord, we [D]offer [Em/B]Thine to be forever,
[C/G]Soul and [G]life and each endeavor.
[G]Thou alone [D7]shall be [G]known [Bm]Lord of all [D7/C]our being,
[Bm]Life's [D7/C]true way decreeing.
